    <statement><p>The function <m>{\bf r} \left( t \right)</m> traces a circle.
Determine the radius, center, and plane containing the circle</p>
<p><m>{\bf r} \left( t \right) = -1 {\bf i} \,  +</m>
<m>\left( 9 \cos(t) \right) {\bf j} \,  +</m>
<m>\left( 9 \sin(t) \right) {\bf k}</m></p>
<p>Plane : <m>x =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p>Circle's Center : ( <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/> , <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0003"/> , <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0004"/> )</p>
<p>Radius : <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0005"/></p>
</statement>
