    <solution><m>x(t) = -1 , y(t) = 9 \cos(t), z(t) = 9 \sin(t)</m>



Hence,



<m>y(t)^2 + z(t)^2 = 81 \cos^2(t) + 81 \sin^2(t) = 81 (\cos^2(t) + \sin^2(t)) = 81</m>



This is the equation of a circle in the vertical plane <m>x = -1</m>. 


The circle is centered at the point <m>(-1 , 0 , 0)</m> and its radius is <m>\sqrt{81} =9</m>



</solution>
